    question: 'What is programming and what is a programming language?', 
    answer: 'Programming is giving instructions to a computer to perform specific tasks. A programming language is a set of rules and syntax to write these instructions in a way computers understand.\n\n🎮 RECIPE ANALOGY:\nProgramming is like cooking:\n- Recipe = Program (instructions)\n- Cooking language (English, French) = Programming Language (Python, Java)\n- Chef = Programmer\n- Dish = Output/Result\n\nTYPES OF PROGRAMMING LANGUAGES:\n📝 High-level: Python, JavaScript (human-readable, easy syntax)\n🔧 Low-level: Assembly, C (closer to machine, more control)\n\n💡 WHY MULTIPLE LANGUAGES?\n- Python: Great for beginners, data science, AI\n- JavaScript: Web development, runs in browsers\n- Java: Enterprise apps, Android\n- C++: Game development, performance-critical\n\n✅ BEST FIRST LANGUAGE FOR FRESHERS:\nPython - simple syntax, huge community, versatile', 
    category: 'Fresher CS Fundamentals', 
    difficulty: 'Easy', 
    tags: ['basics', 'programming'] 
